# What the Docker build is allowed to see.
#
# The build runs `npm ci` itself, so a host node_modules (Windows binaries, possibly stale) must never
# be sent in, and neither must a host dist/ that could mask a failed build.
node_modules
dist
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.vite
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log

# Every .env file, the example included. Vite reads .env, .env.local, .env.production and friends
# from the project root during `vite build` — so a developer's local file would silently bake its
# API URL, or VITE_ALLOW_MOCKS_IN_BUILD, into the image. The image gets its settings from the
# Dockerfile and, at start, from the container environment; nothing else.
.env
.env.*
*.local

# Not needed to build, and changing them should not invalidate the build cache.
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode
docs
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker/test-*.sh
docker/*.mjs
